{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgajEv17aZ8jQCLotx8fz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've proved `revAcc_nil`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nInduction on `xs` doesn't work directly, because the accumulator stops being `[]` after the first step. So I added a more general helper lemma to `Main.lean`:\n\n```lean\ntheorem revAcc_eq (xs acc : List α) : revAcc xs acc = myRev xs ++ acc := by\n  induction xs generalizing acc with\n  | nil => simp [revAcc, myRev]\n  | cons x xs ih => simp [revAcc, myRev, ih]\n\ntheorem revAcc_nil (xs : List α) : revAcc xs [] = myRev xs := by\n  simp [revAcc_eq]\n```\n\n`revAcc_eq` says that `revAcc` with any accumulator gives the reversed list with the accumulator appended. It's proved by induction on `xs`, letting `acc` vary at each step. `revAcc_nil` is then the case where `acc = []`, with `simp` removing the `++ []`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":644,"cache_read_input_tokens":7960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":644},"output_tokens":346,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45b95f2e-3819-4d82-8f79-acfae7cfa042","uuid":"8661882b-8982-4b5e-8c6e-21a897a62515","timestamp":"2026-10-31T17:43:27.479Z","request_id":"req_011CgajEuWMBoFnxnLuChEz8"}
